OK, in the vein of "worst deaths", I think I'll open one for the
"stupidest deaths" category, and put myself up first.  Anyone care
to do better?

BTW, better have some rules - the deaths have to be caused by
honest mistakes (forgetting something is ok), just standing
next to a lizard & having it intentionally beat you up whilst
you do nothing doesn't count.

Righto, on with the show.

Scenario:  Playing a Barbarian (for a change, I prefer casters.  In
fact, I'd just died as a Priest not so long ago on around level 8
of the dungeons of doom).

Up to about level 10, doing ok, nothing fantastic, done the Gnome
mines, on around level 8 of Doom, and find an Altar and a Scroll
in the same room (after knocking off a few monsters).  Sacrifice
the monsters & get my luck up a bit, then ID the scroll - cursed
Scroll of Create Monster - great stuff.  Read the scroll, and
summon a room full of angry monsters.  Start hacking away, going
fairly well, sacrificing every so often & have a couple of artifacts,
plus a few other minor things (can't remember).  Start getting beat
up, so pray on altar and, for once, my luck works - God heals me
up to full & stops the monsters from attacking me whilst I'm
doing it.

Meanwhile, a mummy comes in and joins the fun - whaddya know, it's
my 'ghost' from before, but there's still a few monsters left, so
I forget about it after a time.  Knock off a couple more, including
the Mummy which beat me up pretty badly, so I think "Ho ho, mummy
powerful monster, let's sacrifice ..."  Argh!  All of a sudden,
God very miffed indeed, drains me a level, altar converted and
still a few monsters to go.

Beat up most of them when another few monsters come in, and I'm
getting rather low in the health area, so I think, maybe I'm
forgiven now, let's pray - but I forget, I'm still on the altar...
Super-ARGH!!!  God _extremely_ miffed, drains me another level,
and sends down an avatar to give me what for - two hits later,
and it's "Do you want your possessions identified?" :-( ;-)

So, let's raise the humour level around here, and send in your
groaners.  First prize winner has everyone else on the net send
them email saying "What a LOSER!" :-) :-) :-)

And now for something completely different.

Has anyone noticed how much the altar frequency depends upon your
character class?  Anyone checked the source for this?  When I'm
playing a Wizard, I seem to find altars only one in a blue moon
(excepting Gnome Town) - around one every 100 levels (averaged
over many games).  However, on the opposite end of the spectrum,
when playing a Barbarian it's about when every 5 or 6 levels.
What gives?  I'd think it's hard enough already being a Wizard
without having to worry about finding altars, whereas you'd think
Barbarians & Samurai get it so easy they'd be the ones having
trouble.

